comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-23T18:24:56.022Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: searched all-status PM records for GH-1291, release-workspace-cleanup, Node compile cache and Windows nightly; no item owns this exact September 23 run. Reusing open temp-footprint parent pm-p5u6 and linking the previously completed release-workspace delivery pm-xjy565. Source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1291 and https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/actions/runs/35841395212."
  "2026-09-23T18:25:29.116Z","harness:codex","Investigation: GH #1291 run 35841395212 at bd8942329b8aebbc7482ce6536135535968c0e1d has one failing test, tests/integration/release-workspace-cleanup.integration.spec.ts. The assertion expected only unrelated.txt but saw node-compile-cache under the fixture TEMP/TMP root. Node documentation states module.enableCompileCache without a directory defaults to os.tmpdir()/node-compile-cache, and NODE_DISABLE_COMPILE_CACHE=1 disables it. The directory is a runtime optimization, not an owned release workspace; the fixture should disable it for child processes while still refusing residual owned directories."
